# Rust engine versioning

Index: [changelog](./changelog.mdc) (app releases) · [rust-migration](./rust-migration.mdc)

The Rust engine has its **own** semver. It is **not** the app version (`apps/forja` / `kReleaseCodename` / `vX.Y.Z` tags).

**Current engine version:** `1.2.72`

---

## How to bump (automated)

```bash
./scripts/release_local.sh bump-engine patch|minor|major
```

Updates in one shot:

1. `crates/Cargo.toml` → `[workspace.package] version`
2. `packages/rust/pubspec.yaml` `version:`
3. **Current engine version** in this rule

Does **not** commit, tag, or publish. Commit with the engine PR.

**App release (`release_local` New version / `bump`):** asks “Also bump Rust engine?” (default yes, same patch|minor|major). Skip with answer no or `FORJA_SKIP_ENGINE_BUMP=1`.

---

## Source of truth

| Field | File | Notes |
|-------|------|-------|
| **Engine version** | [`crates/Cargo.toml`](../../crates/Cargo.toml) → `[workspace.package] version` | Only place to bump by hand. Crates use `version.workspace = true`. Boot string is `env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")` via `ffi_version`. |
| **Dart bridge label** | [`packages/rust/pubspec.yaml`](../../packages/rust/pubspec.yaml) `version:` | Kept identical by `bump-engine`. |

Prefer the script over hand-editing.

---

## When to bump

| Bump | Trigger |
|------|---------|
| **patch** | Bug fix, unlock/headers, crash, behavior fix on existing FFI surface |
| **minor** | New FFI / new crate capability; host still works on old symbols |
| **major** | Breaking FFI — deleted/renamed symbols, required host change |

Bump in the PR that lands the change (via `bump-engine`), or at app release if the release includes engine work.

No bump for: docs-only, comment-only, `packages/rust` Dart glue that does not change Rust, or host-only Dart.

---

## What not to do

| Forbidden | Why |
|-----------|-----|
| Invent `engine-v*` git tags (unless we ship a standalone dylib later) | Engine is not a separate download today |
| Edit per-crate `version =` instead of workspace | Breaks single SoT |
| Bump app `pubspec` because crates changed | App patch is a separate admin decision |
| Leave `packages/rust` pubspec behind workspace | Two “engine versions” in the tree |
| Hand-edit only one of the three files | Use `bump-engine` |

---

## User-facing notes (changelog)

If the change is user-visible, add/edit a bullet in the active app [`docs/changelog/*-[draft].md`](../../docs/changelog/) under **Sources**, **Player**, or **Live & IPTV** — same turn as code ([changelog](./changelog.mdc)). No separate engine changelog until we ship the engine as its own artifact.

`bump-engine` does **not** touch the app changelog — you still add the bullet when users would notice.

---

## Checklist (engine PR)

1. `./scripts/release_local.sh bump-engine patch` (or minor/major)
2. Rebuild (`./scripts/build_rust.sh` or CI) so boot log shows the new `Rust engine v…`
3. Changelog bullet if users would notice
4. Commit engine code + version files together
